Z||000003||mshill||10-27-1999||04:19 PM||||Ok, I got an 86 SE V6 that was in excellent condition in and out (except for the typical seat tear on the drivers side) with 188K miles for $750.  I now have put another $1200<BR>into front suspension/brakes/bearings, clutch master, radiator, catatlytic converter, fuel pump/filter, distributor pickup-coil/ignition module/cap/rotor, plugs, wires, coil.<P>So I have about $2000 invested in the car now, but have a large number of brand new parts in it.  I figure I really only needed<BR>about half the stuff that I put in and I bought slightly more expensive/performance parts than stock in some cases (Accel coil and wires, AC Delco Rapid Fire plugs).<P>Granted the car has lower miles, but many rubber items age independently of use (bushings, seals, hoses) and you can bet that  when you do a brake job the rotors/bearings should be replaced as well.<P>If you really want it I wouldn't offer more than $2000 but IMO its a $1500 car max.||||reg||1
